---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base wide title="Gift exchange draw" description="Draw random gift exchange pairings with optional exclusions. Everything stays in your browser.">
  <a class="back" href="/tools/">← Tools</a>
  <h1>Gift exchange draw</h1>
  <p class="muted intro">Make a draw for your group, then tell each person who they got.</p>

  <div class="workspace">
    <form id="draw-form" class="panel">
      <div class="event-field">
        <label for="event-name">Event name</label>
        <input id="event-name" type="text" value="Gift exchange" maxlength="80" autocomplete="off" />
        <p class="helper muted">Used in copied messages. You can change it after drawing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step"><span class="step-number">1</span><h2>People</h2></div>
      <label for="names">One name per line</label>
      <textarea id="names" rows="9" placeholder="Alex&#10;Blair&#10;Casey&#10;Devon" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"></textarea>
      <p class="helper muted">Use distinct names so you know who is who. Everyone gives and receives one gift.</p>

      <div class="step exclusions-heading"><span class="step-number">2</span><h2>Exclusions <span class="optional">optional</span></h2></div>
      <p class="helper muted">Keep two people from drawing each other. Useful for partners or housemates.</p>
      <div class="exclusion-picker">
        <div class="picker-field"><label for="exclude-a">Person</label><select id="exclude-a" disabled></select></div>
        <span class="pair-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↔</span>
        <div class="picker-field"><label for="exclude-b">Cannot draw</label><select id="exclude-b" disabled></select></div>
        <button class="btn add-button" id="add-exclusion" type="button" disabled>Add</button>
      </div>
      <ul id="exclusions" class="exclusion-list" aria-label="Exclusions"></ul>

      <div class="draw-actions">
        <button class="draw-button" type="submit">Draw names <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button>
        <span class="muted draw-note">A new draw replaces the last one.</span>
      </div>
      <p id="feedback" class="feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>

    <section class="panel results-panel" aria-labelledby="results-heading">
      <div class="step"><span class="step-number">3</span><h2 id="results-heading">Pairings</h2></div>
      <div id="empty-results" class="empty-results">
        <svg class="empty-mark" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M24 5v9m0 20v9M5 24h9m20 0h9M10.6 10.6l6.4 6.4m14 14 6.4 6.4m0-26.8L31 17M17 31l-6.4 6.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" />
          <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
        </svg>
        <p>Your pairings will appear here.</p>
        <p class="muted">Only the person viewing this screen can see them. Share each result yourself.</p>
      </div>
      <ol id="results" class="results" hidden></ol>
      <p id="result-note" class="result-note muted" hidden>Names and pairings stay in this tab. Refreshing clears the draw.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <details id="draw-maths" class="draw-maths">
    <summary>How many draws are possible? <span class="muted">A quick explanation and the maths</span></summary>
    <div class="maths-body">
      <dl class="draw-counts">
        <div><dt>People entered</dt><dd id="people-count">0</dd></div>
        <div><dt>No exclusions</dt><dd id="unrestricted-count">Add at least two names</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Exclusion pairs</dt><dd id="exclusion-count">0</dd></div>
        <div><dt>With these exclusions</dt><dd id="restricted-count">Add at least two names</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p id="count-note" class="muted count-note" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

      <section class="explanation" aria-labelledby="plain-heading">
        <h2 id="plain-heading">The short version</h2>
        <p>A draw means the whole set of pairings, not one person's pick. Everyone gives once and receives once. The "No exclusions" total rules out self-draws. The other total also rules out any pair you've excluded.</p>
        <p class="muted">These are counts of possible draws, not odds. The tool finds a valid draw at random, but it does not give every valid draw exactly the same chance.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="explanation" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
        <h2 id="example-heading">A four-person example</h2>
        <p>Say Alex, Blair, Casey, and Devon are exchanging gifts. There are 24 ways to hand out all four names. Once you remove draws where somebody gets their own name, nine remain.</p>
        <ol class="example-steps">
          <li><strong>24</strong><span>ways to hand out four names</span></li>
          <li><strong>9</strong><span>after removing self-draws</span></li>
          <li><strong>4</strong><span>after also excluding Alex and Blair</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p>Why four at the end? Alex and Blair must get Casey and Devon, in either order. Casey and Devon then get Alex and Blair, also in either order. That's 2 × 2 = 4 complete draws.</p>
        <p class="example-result">One of the four: Alex → Casey, Blair → Devon, Casey → Blair, Devon → Alex.</p>
        <p class="muted example-caption">This is a fixed example. The totals above use the names and exclusions you entered.</p>
      </section>

      <details class="technical-details">
        <summary>Show the formulas <span class="muted">For the mathematically curious</span></summary>
        <div class="technical-body">
          <p>Let <i>n</i> be the number of people. Before any restrictions, there are <i>n</i>! assignments. After removing self-draws, the count is called a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derangement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Derangement on Wikipedia, opens in a new tab">derangement</a>.</p>
          <div class="formula">
            <math display="block" aria-label="D sub n equals n factorial times the sum from k equals zero to n of negative one to the k divided by k factorial">
              <msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo>
              <munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover>
              <mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac>
            </math>
          </div>
          <p>For exclusions, mark every self-draw and both directions of each excluded pair as forbidden. Let <i>r</i><sub>k</sub> count the ways to choose <i>k</i> forbidden giver-to-recipient spots without repeating a giver or recipient. <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inclusion%E2%80%93exclusion_principle" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Inclusion-exclusion principle on Wikipedia, opens in a new tab">Inclusion-exclusion</a> then counts the valid draws:</p>
          <div class="formula">
            <math display="block" aria-label="Valid draws equal the sum from k equals zero to n of negative one to the k times r sub k times n minus k factorial">
              <mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo>
              <munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover>
              <msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup>
              <msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub>
              <mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo>
            </math>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">The overlap matters. A complete draw can break several restrictions at once, so subtracting one fixed amount per exclusion would count some draws more than once.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </details>
</Base>

<script>
  import { drawGiftExchange, type Exclusion } from '../../../scripts/giftExchange';
  import { countDerangements, countGiftExchangeDraws } from '../../../scripts/giftExchangeCounts';

  const form = document.getElementById('draw-form') as HTMLFormElement;
  const eventNameInput = document.getElementById('event-name') as HTMLInputElement;
  const namesInput = document.getElementById('names') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
  const selectA = document.getElementById('exclude-a') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const selectB = document.getElementById('exclude-b') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const addButton = document.getElementById('add-exclusion') as HTMLButtonElement;
  const exclusionsList = document.getElementById('exclusions') as HTMLUListElement;
  const feedback = document.getElementById('feedback') as HTMLParagraphElement;
  const results = document.getElementById('results') as HTMLOListElement;
  const emptyResults = document.getElementById('empty-results') as HTMLDivElement;
  const resultNote = document.getElementById('result-note') as HTMLParagraphElement;
  const exclusions = new Set<string>();
  const maths = document.getElementById('draw-maths') as HTMLDetailsElement;
  const peopleCount = document.getElementById('people-count') as HTMLElement;
  const unrestrictedCount = document.getElementById('unrestricted-count') as HTMLElement;
  const exclusionCount = document.getElementById('exclusion-count') as HTMLElement;
  const restrictedCount = document.getElementById('restricted-count') as HTMLElement;
  const countNote = document.getElementById('count-note') as HTMLElement;
  let countTimer = 0;

  const keyFor = (name: string) => name.trim().toLocaleLowerCase();
  const pairKey = (a: string, b: string) => [a, b].sort().join('\u0000');
  const names = () => namesInput.value.split(/\r?\n/).map((name) => name.trim()).filter(Boolean);

  function setFeedback(message: string, error = false) {
    feedback.textContent = message;
    feedback.classList.toggle('error', error);
  }

  function clearResults() {
    results.replaceChildren();
    results.hidden = true;
    resultNote.hidden = true;
    emptyResults.hidden = false;
  }

  function updateCounts() {
    const people = names();
    const count = people.length;
    peopleCount.textContent = String(count);
    exclusionCount.textContent = String(exclusions.size);
    countNote.textContent = '';
    if (count < 2) {
      unrestrictedCount.textContent = 'Add at least two names';
      restrictedCount.textContent = 'Add at least two names';
      return;
    }
    if (count > 100 || new Set(people.map(keyFor)).size !== count) {
      unrestrictedCount.textContent = 'Fix the name list first';
      restrictedCount.textContent = 'Fix the name list first';
      return;
    }

    unrestrictedCount.textContent = countDerangements(count).toLocaleString();
    const indexes = new Map(people.map((name, index) => [keyFor(name), index]));
    const blocked: Exclusion[] = [...exclusions].map((key) => {
      const [a, b] = key.split('\u0000');
      return [indexes.get(a)!, indexes.get(b)!];
    });
    const restricted = countGiftExchangeDraws(count, blocked);
    if (restricted === null) {
      if (drawGiftExchange(count, blocked) === null) {
        restrictedCount.textContent = '0';
        countNote.textContent = 'These exclusions leave no valid draw.';
      } else {
        restrictedCount.textContent = 'Too many linked exclusions to count here';
        countNote.textContent = 'The draw still works. This exact count would take too long in your browser.';
      }
    } else {
      restrictedCount.textContent = restricted.toLocaleString();
    }
  }

  function scheduleCount() {
    if (!maths.open) return;
    window.clearTimeout(countTimer);
    countTimer = window.setTimeout(updateCounts, 120);
  }

  maths.addEventListener('toggle', scheduleCount);

  function renderExclusions(people: string[]) {
    exclusionsList.replaceChildren();
    const display = new Map(people.map((name) => [keyFor(name), name]));
    for (const key of exclusions) {
      const [a, b] = key.split('\u0000');
      if (!display.has(a) || !display.has(b)) {
        exclusions.delete(key);
        continue;
      }
      const item = document.createElement('li');
      const pair = document.createElement('span');
      pair.textContent = `${display.get(a)} ↔ ${display.get(b)}`;
      const remove = document.createElement('button');
      remove.type = 'button';
      remove.className = 'btn remove-button';
      remove.textContent = 'Remove';
      remove.setAttribute('aria-label', `Remove exclusion between ${display.get(a)} and ${display.get(b)}`);
      remove.addEventListener('click', () => {
        exclusions.delete(key);
        renderExclusions(names());
        clearResults();
        setFeedback('');
        scheduleCount();
      });
      item.append(pair, remove);
      exclusionsList.append(item);
    }
  }

  function syncPeople() {
    const people = names();
    const previousA = selectA.value;
    const previousB = selectB.value;
    for (const select of [selectA, selectB]) {
      select.replaceChildren();
      for (const name of people) {
        const option = document.createElement('option');
        option.value = keyFor(name);
        option.textContent = name;
        select.append(option);
      }
      select.disabled = people.length < 2;
    }
    if (people.some((name) => keyFor(name) === previousA)) selectA.value = previousA;
    if (people.some((name) => keyFor(name) === previousB)) selectB.value = previousB;
    else if (people.length > 1) selectB.selectedIndex = 1;
    addButton.disabled = people.length < 2;
    renderExclusions(people);
    clearResults();
    setFeedback('');
    scheduleCount();
  }

  namesInput.addEventListener('input', syncPeople);

  addButton.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (selectA.value === selectB.value) {
      setFeedback('Choose two different people for an exclusion.', true);
      return;
    }
    const key = pairKey(selectA.value, selectB.value);
    if (exclusions.has(key)) {
      setFeedback('That exclusion is already in the list.', true);
      return;
    }
    exclusions.add(key);
    renderExclusions(names());
    clearResults();
    setFeedback('');
    scheduleCount();
  });

  form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    clearResults();
    const people = names();
    if (people.length < 2) {
      setFeedback('Add at least two people to make a draw.', true);
      namesInput.focus();
      return;
    }
    if (people.length > 100) {
      setFeedback('This draw supports up to 100 people.', true);
      namesInput.focus();
      return;
    }
    if (people.some((name) => name.length > 60)) {
      setFeedback('Keep each name to 60 characters or fewer.', true);
      namesInput.focus();
      return;
    }
    if (new Set(people.map(keyFor)).size !== people.length) {
      setFeedback('Each name must be unique. Add a surname or initial to repeated names.', true);
      namesInput.focus();
      return;
    }

    const indexes = new Map(people.map((name, index) => [keyFor(name), index]));
    const blocked: Exclusion[] = [...exclusions].map((key) => {
      const [a, b] = key.split('\u0000');
      return [indexes.get(a)!, indexes.get(b)!];
    });
    const draw = drawGiftExchange(people.length, blocked);
    if (!draw) {
      setFeedback('No valid draw is possible with these exclusions. Remove one or more and try again.', true);
      return;
    }

    draw.forEach((recipientIndex, giverIndex) => {
      const item = document.createElement('li');
      const pairing = document.createElement('span');
      pairing.className = 'pairing';
      const giver = document.createElement('strong');
      giver.textContent = people[giverIndex];
      const arrow = document.createElement('span');
      arrow.className = 'result-arrow';
      arrow.textContent = '→';
      arrow.setAttribute('aria-label', 'gives to');
      const recipient = document.createElement('strong');
      recipient.textContent = people[recipientIndex];
      pairing.append(giver, arrow, recipient);
      const copy = document.createElement('button');
      copy.type = 'button';
      copy.className = 'btn copy-button';
      copy.textContent = 'Copy message';
      copy.setAttribute('aria-label', `Copy message for ${people[giverIndex]}`);
      copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          const eventName = eventNameInput.value.trim() || 'Gift exchange';
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(`Hi ${people[giverIndex]}! For ${eventName}, you're giving a gift to ${people[recipientIndex]}.`);
          copy.textContent = 'Copied';
          setFeedback(`Copied ${people[giverIndex]}'s message.`);
          window.setTimeout(() => { copy.textContent = 'Copy message'; }, 2000);
        } catch {
          setFeedback('Could not copy. You can select the names from the pairing list instead.', true);
        }
      });
      item.append(pairing, copy);
      results.append(item);
    });
    emptyResults.hidden = true;
    results.hidden = false;
    resultNote.hidden = false;
    setFeedback(`Draw complete for ${people.length} people.`);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .back { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.5rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: .92rem; }
  h1 { margin: 1.2rem 0 .3rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .intro { margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
  .workspace { display: grid; gap: 1rem; align-items: start; max-width: 70rem; }
  .panel { min-width: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; background: var(--surface); padding: clamp(1.15rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); }
  .event-field { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .step { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .7rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .step-number { display: grid; place-items: center; flex: 0 0 1.85rem; height: 1.85rem; border-radius: 50%; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, var(--surface)); color: var(--accent); font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 700; }
  h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--fg); text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; font-size: 1.16rem; }
  label { display: block; font-weight: 600; font-size: .88rem; margin-bottom: .35rem; }
  input, textarea, select { width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: inherit; }
  input { min-height: 2.75rem; padding: .5rem .8rem; }
  textarea { display: block; padding: .7rem .8rem; resize: vertical; min-height: 11rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  textarea::placeholder { color: var(--muted); opacity: .7; }
  select { height: 2.55rem; padding: 0 .65rem; }
  .helper { margin: .5rem 0 0; font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .exclusions-heading { margin: 2rem 0 .25rem; }
  .optional { color: var(--muted); font-size: .83rem; font-weight: 400; }
  .exclusion-picker { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: .55rem; align-items: end; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .picker-field { min-width: 0; }
  .pair-symbol { align-self: end; padding-bottom: .5rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .add-button { min-height: 2.55rem; }
  button:disabled, select:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; opacity: .55; }
  .exclusion-list { display: grid; gap: .45rem; padding: 0; margin: .8rem 0 0; list-style: none; }
  .exclusion-list:empty { display: none; }
  .exclusion-list :global(li) { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; padding: .3rem .35rem .3rem .75rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; font-size: .9rem; }
  .exclusion-list :global(.remove-button) { font-size: .78rem; padding: .2rem .65rem; }
  .draw-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .8rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .draw-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg); padding: .65rem 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .draw-button:hover { filter: brightness(1.12); }
  .draw-note { font-size: .8rem; }
  .feedback { min-height: 1.5em; margin: .8rem 0 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: .88rem; }
  .feedback.error { color: #bd594f; }
  .empty-results { text-align: center; padding: 3rem 1rem 3.5rem; }
  .empty-mark { display: block; width: 3rem; height: 3rem; margin-inline: auto; color: var(--accent); }
  .empty-results p { margin: .8rem 0 0; }
  .empty-results p:last-child { font-size: .88rem; }
  .results { display: grid; gap: .55rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .results :global(li) { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .6rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: .65rem .75rem; }
  .results :global(.pairing) { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .55rem; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .results :global(.result-arrow) { color: var(--accent); }
  .results :global(.copy-button) { font-size: .78rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .result-note { margin: 1rem 0 0; font-size: .82rem; }
  .draw-maths { max-width: 70rem; margin-top: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; background: var(--surface); }
  .draw-maths summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 1rem 1.4rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .draw-maths summary::marker { color: var(--accent); }
  .draw-maths summary .muted { margin-left: .35rem; font-size: .84rem; font-weight: 400; }
  .maths-body { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.2rem clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.8rem) 1.6rem; max-width: 54rem; }
  .draw-counts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .65rem; margin: 0; }
  .draw-counts div { min-width: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: .7rem .8rem; }
  .draw-counts dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; }
  .draw-counts dd { margin: .15rem 0 0; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.35; overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .count-note { min-height: 1.3em; margin: .7rem 0 0; font-size: .85rem; }
  .explanation { margin-top: 1.7rem; }
  .maths-body h2 { margin: 0 0 .55rem; }
  .maths-body p { max-width: 48rem; font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .explanation p { margin: .55rem 0; }
  .example-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .55rem; padding: 0; margin: 1rem 0; list-style: none; }
  .example-steps li { display: grid; align-content: start; gap: .2rem; min-width: 0; padding: .75rem .85rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; }
  .example-steps strong { color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.45rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; line-height: 1.2; }
  .example-steps span { color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .example-result { padding: .7rem .85rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 6%, var(--surface)); }
  .example-caption { font-size: .8rem !important; }
  .technical-details { margin-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .technical-details summary { padding: 1rem 0; font-size: .92rem; }
  .technical-details summary .muted { font-size: .82rem; }
  .technical-body { padding: .1rem 0 .2rem; }
  .technical-body p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .formula { overflow-x: auto; padding: .65rem 0; color: var(--fg); }
  .formula math { font-size: 1.14rem; }
  @media (min-width: 55rem) { .workspace { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, .9fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 32rem) {
    .exclusion-picker { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .add-button { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .draw-counts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .example-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .draw-maths summary .muted { display: block; margin-left: 1.1rem; }
  }
</style>
